      "writtenOn": "2026-03-25T20:25:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the details! The issue was a missing R32Float case in the CheckFourColors switch — the depth/disparity formats that map to R32Float would enter the render tests and hit DAWN_UNREACHABLE() at line 780.\n\nI couldn\u0027t reproduce locally because my CMake build didn\u0027t have DAWN_ALWAYS_ASSERT enabled, so the assertion was silently a no-op. PS4 adds the missing switch case.\n\n(Note: this is technically a pre-existing gap — OneComponent32Float also maps to R32Float and is renderable, so it could have hit the same path.)",
      "parentUuid": "0617e937_aad777ae",
      "revId": "992841648b6a067353a2860db6e2e16019e84ba3",
